RATIONALE: The L0 simulation is a structurally rigorous evaluation (24 seeds, Bonferroni FWER, service-time feedback loop) that successfully avoided the prior FCFS strawman and yielded an honest, definitive negative on the joint-dominance claim. This is a highly valuable, valid outcome that closes the reframe. I vote green to accept the negative. However, the simulation remains a toy abstraction; the proposed pivot to multi-SLO priority classes MUST abandon the CPU simulation and be evaluated on real GPU schedulers, as real prefill costs and batching are deeply non-linear.
